{"kind":"assert","text":"A second question for the cutover head (05d618e2). At this head, install refuses the maintained Grow application. WIP head bbc17b2a.\n\nThe scope archive failures are down from 65 to 10 of 189. Three of the 10 wait on genesis-anchor question 1cf42f3b. The other 7 are all Grow install scenarios: five refuse install_application with invalid-application-package, and the Grow public archive command fails after them.\n\nThe cause: cutover commit 23e0c92d (\"Compose the reviewed identifier source components\") brought { canonical: true } into all four install validators:\n- application-install.ts:103\n- application-install-v2.ts:40\n- device-application-rules.ts:51\n- validate-package.ts:28\nMain has none of these. The Grow grow-room declaration fails canonical mode with \"must omit redundant subjects and empty optional filters\". That holds for the live examples/grow packet and for the retained declaration, and the cutover changed neither. The flag came in through a composed component. I have not found a ruling that requires canonical install for the identifier cutover.\n\nChoose one:\n(i) Drop canonical mode from install validation, back to main. Canonical install becomes its own request.\n(ii) Keep it, and re-spell grow-room canonically. That changes the grow-room digest, the demo release, and the retained pin fixture that tests history.\n(iii) Keep it for new packages only, and admit packages already released as they are.\n\nI recommend (i). Identifiers do not need canonical install, and (ii) changes a released application's digest inside the cutover. If you ruled canonical install into one of the composed components, name the ruling and I take (ii) or (iii) as you say.\n\nAlso, three behaviour faults so far share one cause: a comparison of seed.creator with a full sequence reference, where the creator makes the seed in its own genesis and so names itself {scope, genesis: null}. They are publishing-provenance installedApplicationOrigin and act-admission.ts sibling and ancestor checks. The lane fixed all three with resolveGenesisSelf. The idle lane now audits every remaining same(seed.creator, ...) comparison read-only, and the cutover lane fixes each fault found before the gate."}